@lc8882972 just do this:

`OPENCODE_EXPERIMENTAL_NATIVE_LLM=0`

If u have that env var set this code path isnt ever hit (it isnt hit by default but this will ensure its not hit otherwise either).

> I have similar issue:
> 
> (base) PS C:\Users\Romy1> opencode mcp auth drive
> 
> T MCP OAuth Authentication | o Authentication successful! | — Done
> 
> (base) PS C:\Users\Romy1> opencode mcp auth list
> 
> T MCP OAuth Status | • ✗ drive not authenticated | https://drivemcp.googleapis.com/mcp/v1 | — 1 OAuth-capable server(s)

I was able to fix this by using the following script. 
prior to that I make sure I logout from the mcp using;
`opencode mcp logout google-drive-mcp`

Script:
`` 
<#
.SYNOPSIS
Configure and authenticate OpenCode's Google Drive MCP server.

.DESCRIPTION
OpenCode currently can report Google Drive MCP as connected before OAuth tokens
are stored, because the Drive MCP endpoint allows the initial MCP handshake
without user authorization. This script performs the Google OAuth flow directly,
then writes tokens to OpenCode's MCP auth store in the format OpenCode expects.

Required environment variables:
  GOOGLE_DRIVE_MCP_CLIENT_ID
  GOOGLE_DRIVE_MCP_CLIENT_SECRET

After this script succeeds, restart OpenCode so the running MCP client reloads
the token from ~/.local/share/opencode/mcp-auth.json.
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [string]$ServerName = "drive",
    [string]$ServerUrl = "https://drivemcp.googleapis.com/mcp/v1",
    [int]$CallbackPort = 19876,
    [string]$CallbackPath = "/mcp/oauth/callback",
    [string]$ConfigPath = (Join-Path $HOME ".config\opencode\opencode.json"),
    [string]$AuthPath = (Join-Path $HOME ".local\share\opencode\mcp-auth.json"),
    [switch]$SkipConfigUpdate
)

$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

$Scopes = @(
    "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly",
    "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file"
)
$Scope = $Scopes -join " "

function New-Base64UrlRandomString {
    param([int]$ByteCount = 32)

    $bytes = New-Object byte[] $ByteCount
    [System.Security.Cryptography.RandomNumberGenerator]::Create().GetBytes($bytes)
    return [Convert]::ToBase64String($bytes).TrimEnd("=").Replace("+", "-").Replace("/", "_")
}

function ConvertTo-Base64UrlSha256 {
    param([Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$Value)

    $sha = [System.Security.Cryptography.SHA256]::Create()
    $hash = $sha.ComputeHash([System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetBytes($Value))
    return [Convert]::ToBase64String($hash).TrimEnd("=").Replace("+", "-").Replace("/", "_")
}

function ConvertTo-UrlEncoded {
    param([Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$Value)

    return [Uri]::EscapeDataString($Value)
}

function Ensure-Directory {
    param([Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$Path)

    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Path)) {
        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $Path | Out-Null
    }
}

function Add-OrSetProperty {
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]$Object,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$Name,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]$Value
    )

    if ($Object.PSObject.Properties.Name -contains $Name) {
        $Object.$Name = $Value
    }
    else {
        $Object | Add-Member -NotePropertyName $Name -NotePropertyValue $Value
    }
}

function Write-JsonFile {
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$Path,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]$Value
    )

    Ensure-Directory -Path (Split-Path -Parent $Path)
    $Value | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 20 | Set-Content -LiteralPath $Path -Encoding UTF8
}

